1
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,060
We were wondering what was taking so long...

2
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,240
...but now we understand. You were doing this.

3
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:23,400
Okay. I wanted to surprise you, but....

4
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,840
For your housewarming gift,

5
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,080
I got you a baby chick and a baby duck.

6
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,380
Really? You got us a chick and a duck?

7
00:00:30,956 --> 00:00:32,246
Oh, great.

8
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:32,900
Just what you want for

9
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:35,560
a new house with infants. Bird feces!

10
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,380
But they must've jumped off the table.

11
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,340
Now they're gone!

12
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,660
Don't worry, we'll find them.

13
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,140
Actually, I'm gonna go check on the twins.

14
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:45,700
Oh, God! What did I just step on?

15
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:48,680
It's okay. It's just an egg roll.

16
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,260
You stepped on my egg roll?!

17
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,120
I'm sorry.

18
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,400
I didn't know to look for Chinese food on the floor.

19
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:57,780
Just put it on a plate and leave.

20
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,040
- Okay. Let's find these birds. - All right.

21
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,040
Wait, wait. You hear that?

22
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,620
They're in the table!

23
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,440
Well, that can't be good.

24
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,700
- We gotta get them out of there! - How?

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,580
Maybe we can lure them out. You know any birdcalls?

26
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:25,760
Oh, tons. I'm quite the woodsman.

27
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,860
Well, maybe we can just tip the table a little.

28
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:32,820
Joey, wait! The ball!

29
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,340
So, what do we do?

30
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,840
Maybe we can open this up somehow.

31
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:54,420
Okay.

32
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,560
No. It's all glued together.

33
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,000
Does that mean we have to bust it open?

34
00:02:03,587 --> 00:02:07,440
- I don't know. Maybe. - Oh, my God.

35
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,790
I know. It's-- It's the foosball table.

36
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,540
All right, you know what? We don't have a choice.

37
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,560
It's like I would have said in that sci-fi movie

38
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,580
if I'd have gotten the part.

39
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:24,380
Those are our men in there, and we have to get them out...

40
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,920
...even if I have to sacrifice the most important thing in my life...

41
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,660
...my time machine.

42
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:35,320
- Did that movie ever get made? - It did not.

43
00:02:42,947 --> 00:02:44,127
Ross, where are you going?

44
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:45,560
To talk to Rachel.

45
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,660
Isn't that why we took a ride in the death cab?

46
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,420
You're walking up to her at the gate?

47
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:53,140
Have you never chased anyone through the airport before?

48
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,780
Not since my cop show got canceled.

49
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:58,900
You have to get a ticket to get past security.

50
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,420
What? We're never gonna make it.

51
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:02,740
Not with that attitude. Now, haul ass!

52
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,560
Okay, if you could all walk slower,

53
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:08,620
that'd be great.

54
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,760
- Madame, your passport, please. - Oh, my God.

55
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,100
I was afraid I wouldn't remember my high school French.

56
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,200
But I understood every word you just said.

57
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,780
- Your boarding pass, please. - Oh, sure.

58
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:35,960
Shoot, I had it. Oh, I can't believe this.

59
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:37,460
Madame, if you don't have your--

60
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,120
I have it, I have it!

61
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:42,720
Okay, I can't find it,

62
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:46,280
but I remember that I was in seat 32C...

63
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,180
...because that's my bra size.

64
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,660
Madame. You must have your boarding pass--

65
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,740
Ok, fine. But you know what?

66
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:55,540
If I was in 36D, we would not be having this problem.

67
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,300
- Hi. I need a ticket. - Just one?

68
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,440
I drive you here,

69
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,300
and I don't get to see how it works out?

70
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,800
Fine. Two tickets. I need two tickets.

71
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,200
We're on our honeymoon.

72
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:15,740
And the destination?

73
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,420
I don't care. Whatever's the cheapest.

74
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,020
I'm so lucky I married you.

75
00:04:23,527 --> 00:04:27,187
Oh, shoot. Damn it. Where is it?

76
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:31,460
I found it. I found it. I told you I would find it.

77
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:33,400
In your face. You're a different person.

78
00:04:35,686 --> 00:04:37,356
Sorry.

79
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:40,080
Okay. Flight 421, Paris.

80
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,300
I don't see it. Do you see it?

81
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,560
No. Did we miss it?

82
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:47,200
No, no, it's impossible. It doesn't leave for another 20 minutes.

83
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,640
Maybe we have the flight number wrong.

84
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:51,380
God.

85
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,100
- Hello. - Hey, it's me. Here's Ross.

86
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,550
What?

87
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,780
Hey. Hey, listen--

88
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,040
You wouldn't believe the cute noises the twins are making.

89
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:05,040
Wait, listen.

90
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:05,620
But Monica--

91
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,340
Monica...

92
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,820
I'm sorry. They were doing it before.

93
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:15,880
That's all right. Listen, listen.

94
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,820
Oh, wait, wait. Here they go again.

95
00:05:18,907 --> 00:05:23,137
Monica...

96
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,600
- <i>Monica?</i> - Isn't that cute?

97
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,080
That is precious! Listen....

98
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:29,960
I need Rachel's flight information.

99
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:30,740
<i>Oh, okay.</i>

100
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:35,160
All right, it's flight 421. Leaves at 8:40.

101
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:37,280
Yes, that's what I had . It's not on the board.

102
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,240
That's what it says here.

103
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,280
Flight 421. Leaves at 8:40. Newark Airport.

104
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,580
- What? - <i>Newark Airport.</i>

105
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,460
Why? Where are you?

106
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:47,900
JFK.

107
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,480
Don't worry, you guys!

108
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,140
We're gonna get you out of there!

109
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,700
And we're also gonna buy you tiny bird hearing aids.

110
00:06:32,132 --> 00:06:35,072
Okay. Here goes.

111
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:40,840
What's the matter?

112
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,160
I need to say goodbye to the table first.

113
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:48,480
I understand.

114
00:06:50,509 --> 00:06:51,869
Okay.

115
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,920
Table...

116
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:03,020
...you have given us so many great times.

117
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:09,740
And you guys, Jordan, Victor, Joel....

118
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,520
All of you guys. What can I say?

119
00:07:15,133 --> 00:07:20,613
You guys make us look good.

120
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,840
- You want to say anything? - I don't know.

121
00:07:28,429 --> 00:07:32,439
Except that, for one last time....

122
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:38,090
Good game...

123
00:07:39,885 --> 00:07:41,335
Good game.

124
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:45,960
Okay. Here we go.

125
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:56,400
I can't do it.

126
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,080
Well, I can't do it either.

127
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:01,740
Hey. Did you find them?

128
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,900
Yeah. They're stuck inside the table.

129
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,400
And we have to bust it open, but neither of us can do it.

130
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:10,520
Oh, well, sure. It's got to be so hard.

131
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,340
I'll do it. Give me.

132
00:08:19,267 --> 00:08:20,827
Phoebe!

133
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:21,800
No, no, no!

134
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:26,620
Wow, I've never gone this fast before.

135
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:28,920
Phoebe, forget it, okay?

136
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,860
Newark is, like, an hour away.

137
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,680
There's no way we'll make it in time.

138
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,580
She's got her cell. You could call her.

139
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,560
I am not doing this over the phone.

140
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,340
You don't have any other choice.

141
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,820
- Hello? - Rachel. Oh, good.

142
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,060
By the way, did you just get on the plane?

143
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:52,320
- Yeah. - For what is worse, we would have caught her...

144
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:53,500
...if we were at the right airport.

145
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,840
- Rachel, hang on. - <i>No. No. No.</i>

146
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:02,520
Phoebe, is everything okay?

147
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:09,520
Actually, no. No. You have to get off the plane.

148
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:12,340
- What? Why? - I have this feeling that...

149
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,460
...something's wrong with it.

150
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:17,300
Something is wrong with the left phalange.

151
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:22,400
Oh, honey, I'm sure there's nothing wrong with the plane.

152
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,020
Look, I have to go.

153
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:27,000
I love you, and l will call you the minute I get to Paris.

154
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:31,580
What was that?

155
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:34,240
Oh, that was just my crazy friend.

156
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,760
She told me to get off the plane

157
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:37,920
because she had a "feeling" that there...

158
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,940
...was something wrong with the left phalange.

159
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:43,980
Okay. That doesn't sound good.

160
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,980
Oh, I wouldn't worry about it.

161
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,440
She comes up with this stuff,

162
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,680
and she's almost never right.

163
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,060
But she is sometimes.

164
00:09:50,913 --> 00:09:52,273
Well....

165
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:54,780
What are you doing?

166
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,280
I can't take this plane now.

167
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,000
Excuse me, sir. Where are you going?

168
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,200
I have to get off this plane.

169
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:02,020
Her friend has a feeling

170
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,820
something's wrong with the left phalange.

171
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,580
Could I get some peanuts?

172
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,320
What's wrong with the plane?

173
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:13,300
There's nothing wrong.

174
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,660
The left phalange.

175
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,620
There's no "phalange."

176
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,020
Oh, my God. This plane doesn't even have a phalange.

177
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:24,000
- I'm not flying on it. - Ma'am. Please sit down.

178
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:24,780
What's going on?

179
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,360
We're getting off. There is no phalange!

180
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,780
This is ridiculous. I--

181
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,760
Yeah, okay.

182
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,560
All right. My job here is done.

183
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:53,260
That was impressive.

184
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,960
Yeah. You didn't even use the tools for most of it.

185
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:00,220
Yeah, they were just slowing me down.

186
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,240
All right. I gotta get back to the babies.

187
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:04,840
See you girls later.

188
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:12,320
- Sorry about the table, man. - Yeah.

189
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:14,420
You gonna buy a new one?

190
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,420
Probably not. No.

191
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,160
I don't know how much I'm gonna want to play

192
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:20,960
after you go.

193
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,020
- At least we got these little guys out. - Yeah.

194
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,660
We were worried about you.

195
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,240
I guess I better get used to things

196
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,660
crapping in my hand, huh?

197
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,960
I'm gonna miss these little guys.

198
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,480
It was nice having birds around again.

199
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,480
Hey, you know what?

200
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,860
Maybe we should keep them here with you.

201
00:11:59,060 --> 00:11:59,890
What?

202
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,900
Yeah. We got a lot going on right now.

203
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,920
And plus, here, they'd have their own room.

204
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,320
I could get a goose!

205
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,300
You know, I think you're set with the poultry.

206
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:18,320
Thanks, man. You hear that, you guys?

207
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,580
You're gonna get to stay here.

208
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:22,565
And it's good...

209
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:23,200
...you know, because....

210
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:26,600
Because now you have a reason

211
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,220
to come visit.

212
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,120
I think there may be another reason.

213
00:12:42,378 --> 00:12:43,788
So....

214
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:49,460
Awkward hug or lame cool-guy handshake?

215
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:52,400
Yeah, well, you know,

216
00:12:52,420 --> 00:12:54,080
lame cool-guy handshake.

217
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,720
Ma'am, I assure you, the plane is fine.

218
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:17,460
And you fixed the phalange?

219
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,200
Yes. The phalange's fixed.

220
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:22,210
As a matter of fact,

221
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,040
we've put a whole lot of extra phalanges onboard,

222
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:24,840
just in case.

223
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,080
- Where is she? - I don't see her.

224
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:35,620
- Rachel! Rachel Green! - There she is!

225
00:13:36,161 --> 00:13:39,001
Rachel! Rachel!

226
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:40,820
Whoa, do you have a boarding pass?

227
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,480
No. I just have to talk to someone.

228
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,680
I'm sorry. You need a boarding pass.

229
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,180
- No, no. But you don't-- - Rachel!

230
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:51,960
What? Oh, my God.

231
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:53,740
What are you guys doing here?

232
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,940
Okay. You're on.

233
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:57,420
What? What, Ross?

234
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,140
Okay, you're scaring me. What's going on?

235
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,720
- Okay. Thing is.... - Yeah.

236
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,800
- Don't go. - What?

237
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,740
Please, please stay with me.

238
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:10,980
I am so in love with you. Please don't go.

239
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,640
- Oh, my God. - I know. I know.

240
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:16,660
I shouldn't have waited till now to say it,

241
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:19,700
but-- That was stupid, okay? I'm sorry.

242
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,120
But I'm telling you now.

243
00:14:21,530 --> 00:14:22,440
I love you.

244
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,260
Do not get on this plane.

245
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:28,400
Miss, are you boarding the plane?

246
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:30,080
Hey, hey.

247
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:34,880
I know you love me. I know you do.

248
00:14:37,719 --> 00:14:39,469
- Miss. - I....

249
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:41,040
l.... I have to get on the plane.

250
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,600
- No, you don't. - Yes, I do.

251
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,360
- No, you don't. I do. - They're waiting for me, Ross.

252
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,440
I can't do this right now,

253
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:48,500
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

254
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:50,640
Rachel.

255
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,240
I'm so sorry.

256
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:09,900
I really thought she'd stay.

257
00:15:10,009 --> 00:15:11,519
I know.

258
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,060
I'm sorry.

259
00:15:27,547 --> 00:15:30,737
Well, that's it.

260
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:32,040
Everything's packed.

261
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,180
This is weird.

262
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,110
I know.

263
00:15:39,364 --> 00:15:40,714
Yeah.

264
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:42,820
Does this mean there's nothing to eat?

265
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:47,140
I put three lasagnas in your freezer.

266
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,040
I love you.

267
00:15:54,374 --> 00:15:55,234
Hey.

268
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,300
Hey. Did you guys make it in time?

269
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:57,960
Yeah, yeah.

270
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,640
He talked to her, but she got on the plane anyway.

271
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:04,360
Where's Ross?

272
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:06,840
He went home. He didn't want to see anybody.

273
00:16:25,448 --> 00:16:28,968
<i>Ross. Hi, it's me.</i>

274
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:31,060
<i>I just got back on the plane,</i>

275
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,220
<i>and I just feel awful.</i>

276
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:36,620
<i>That is so not how I wanted</i>

277
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:38,540
<i>things to end with us.</i>

278
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:42,600
<i>It's just that I wasn't expecting</i>

279
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,340
<i>to see you.</i>

280
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:45,140
<i>And all of a sudden you're there</i>

281
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:46,700
<i>and saying these things.</i>

282
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:49,940
<i>Now I'm just sitting here</i>

283
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:50,640
<i>and thinking...</i>

284
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,260
<i>...of all the stuff I should have said</i>

285
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:54,200
<i>and I didn't.</i>

286
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:57,060
<i>I mean, I didn't even get to tell you</i>

287
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:58,520
<i>that I love you too.</i>

288
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:03,600
<i>Because of course I do. I love you.</i>

289
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:06,320
<i>I love you.</i>

290
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:09,180
<i>I love you.</i>

291
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:14,000
<i>What am I doing? I love you.</i>

292
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,060
<i>I've got to see you.</i>

293
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:19,840
<i>I've got to get off this plane.</i>

294
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,040
Oh, my God.

295
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,540
<i>Okay, excuse me.</i>

296
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,892
<i>Miss, please sit down.</i>

297
00:17:24,912 --> 00:17:26,580
<i>No, I'm sorry. I'm really sorry,</i>

298
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,500
<i>but I need to get off the plane.</i>

299
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:30,220
<i>I need to tell someone that I love them.</i>

300
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,600
<i>Miss, I can't let you off.</i>

301
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,440
Let her off the plane!

302
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:37,560
<i>I am afraid you are gonna have to take a seat.</i>

303
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:39,980
<i>Oh, please, Miss.</i> <i>You don't understand.</i>

304
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:41,300
Try to understand!

305
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,880
<i>Come on, miss, isn't there any way</i>

306
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,340
<i>that you can just let me off the</i>--<i>?</i>

307
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:47,920
No! No!

308
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,840
Oh, my God. Did she get off the plane?

309
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,160
Did she get off the plane?

310
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:57,260
I got off the plane.

311
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:09,620
You got off the plane.

312
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,980
I do love you.

313
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,000
I love you too,

314
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,140
and I am never letting you go again.

315
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,100
Okay. Because this is where I want to be.

316
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,480
No more messing around.

317
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,760
I don't want to mess this up again.

318
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:36,180
Me neither. We're done being stupid.

319
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,800
Okay. It's you and me, all right? This is it.

320
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,220
This is it. Unless we're on a break.

321
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,880
Don't make jokes now.

322
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,800
Okay, please be careful with that.

323
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,600
It was my grandmother's. Be careful.

324
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:18,980
Thank you.

325
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,140
If that falls off the truck,

326
00:19:21,250 --> 00:19:22,440
it wouldn't be the worst thing.

327
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,100
I know.

328
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,680
Seems smaller somehow.

329
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:43,660
Has it always been purple?

330
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,800
Look around, you guys.

331
00:19:49,550 --> 00:19:51,220
This was your first home.

332
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:54,440
And it was a happy place,

333
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:57,720
filled with love and laughter.

334
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,920
But more important,

335
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:02,540
because of rent control, it was a frigging steal.

336
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:10,440
Hey, do you realize that, at one time or another,

337
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,340
we all lived in this apartment?

338
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:15,000
Oh, yeah. That's true.

339
00:20:15,361 --> 00:20:17,371
I haven't.

340
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:20,780
What about that summer during college

341
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:21,800
that you lived with Grandma...

342
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,900
...and you tried to make it as a dancer?

343
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:31,960
Do you realize we almost made it 10 years

344
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,160
without that coming up?

345
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:38,880
Oh, honey, I forgot.

346
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:41,180
I promised Treeger that we'd leave our keys.

347
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:41,980
Oh, okay.

348
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,860
- So I guess this is it. - Yeah.

349
00:21:22,380 --> 00:21:23,260
I guess so.

350
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:27,780
This is harder than I thought it would be.

351
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:29,860
Oh, it's gonna be okay.

352
00:21:33,807 --> 00:21:35,177
Come on.

353
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,180
Do you guys have to go to the new house now,

354
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:45,760
or do you have some time?

355
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,500
We got some time.

356
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:54,200
- Okay. Should we get some coffee? - Sure.

357
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,180
Where?

